## 5. Escalation YAML files and handler classes

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/` — each YAML maps an exception FQN to a handler class:

| YAML file | Handler |
|---|---|
| `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.RequiredFieldsException.yml` | `RequiredFieldsExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` |

Each YAML is just:
```yaml
handle:
  class: <handler FQN>
```

Handler classes are in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`. Key ones:

**`RequiredFieldsException.java`** — carries a `List<String> errors`; `getErrors()`.

**`RequiredFieldsExceptionHandler.java`** — returns **400** with `ValidationErrorsResponse`:
```java
public void handle(@Parameter RequiredFieldsException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ValidationErrorsResponse>> response) {
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
            .body(new ValidationErrorsResponse(ex.getErrors())));
}
```

**`ValidationErrorsResponse.java`** — serializes as `{"errors": [...]}` (final `List<String> errors`, `getErrors()`).

**`DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler.java`** — note it returns **NOT_FOUND (404)**, not 409:
```java
public void handle(@Parameter DataIntegrityViolationException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response) {
    ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND,
            "The requested resource could not be processed due to a data constraint violation");
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(detail));
}
```

**`NotFoundExceptionHandler.java`** — 404 empty body. **`ForbiddenExceptionHandler.java`** — 403 ProblemDetail (`AuthorizationDeniedException`). **`GeneralExceptionHandler.java`** — 500 ProblemDetail. **`ValidationExceptionHandler.java`** — 400 ProblemDetail with `schemaValidationErrors` list (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`). **`ProblemDetails.java`** — shared builder (title = exception simple name, timestamp, empty `schemaValidationErrors`). `NotFoundException.java` — simple `extends Exception`.

There is currently **no** escalation YAML/handler that produces HTTP **409 Conflict**.

---

## 6. Existing telephone normalization logic

The only normalization logic in the codebase is in **`RequireOwnerFields.java`** (lines 33–38, shown above): `request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "")`, then require exactly 10 digits (else `RequiredFieldsException(List.of("telephone"))`), then `request.setTelephone(telephone)`.

Other telephone references are non-normalization:
- `Owner.java` — the field + `@Pattern("^[0-9]{10}$")`.
- `ApplyOwner.java` (line 14, `owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone())`) — used by the PUT/update pipeline, not POST.
- JDBC repo SQL column lists in `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl.java`.

No `normalize`/`normalise` method exists anywhere; no shared telephone utility class.

---

## 7. Existing owner-creation tests

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — black-box tests hitting `POST /api/owners`:
```java
/** telephone-unique: Reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by any other owner. Re... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());   // expects 409
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
		createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
		createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```
These tests expect a **telephone-uniqueness rule returning 409 Conflict** — which is not yet implemented (no uniqueness check in the pipeline/repository, and the only data-integrity handler returns 404).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — test harness (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`). Key helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner; `uniqueTelephone()` returns `"04"+8 digits` (10 digits); `createOwner(body)` POSTs to `/api/owners`; `createOwnerOk`, `createOwnerWithKey` (with `Idempotency-Key` header), `getOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `extractId`. Also pinned reference data (CITY_REGION, REGION_TIMEZONE, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS) and `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` helpers, suggesting a broader spec chain of owner-create rules.

Also present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (matched the test grep; audit-log capture support).

